mh2lm: prove SPI 513 delivery before arming PMIC key IRQs (0135)

The 0114a9 Power trial stopped because the non-secure GICD_IGROUPR readback
remained zero. Earlier shim work showed that readback is not by itself a
reliable delivery check. Keep the Group 1 write, configuration readbacks and
hardware gate ordering, but software-pend SPI 513 with PDC disabled before
opening any PMIC gate. Accept hardware mode only after sleh_irq observes one
bounded probe hit and the pending/active state clears. On failure, leave the
20 ms key poller in place. The established USB CDC-ACM console is enabled by
the packaging profile for live diagnostics.

